node_modules/
dist/
/out/
data/
!/hswarm/data/
*.log
# Python's bytecode cache is machine-local. An untracked one reads as a dirty tree, and the live
# checkout's updater refuses a dirty tree (hswarm/__pycache__ held every update, 2026-10-03).
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local
# Local AI working state stays local (codemap index, memory, launch config, harnesses) - but the
# SLASH COMMANDS ship: they are how a person operates this daemon, and a rule that lives on one
# machine is not a rule the team has. Same idiom as .arkitect below.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/commands/
# Architect: run output stays local; the config + custom checks (your-checks/) are committed
# owner-owned tooling (the reusable guardrail checks live there). The core is fetched by npx.
.arkitect/*
!.arkitect/arkitect.config.json
!.arkitect/your-checks/
tmp/
# SUE and Dredd records (simulated-visitor runs, rounds, rulings) stay on the machine that ran them.
/.sue/
/.dredd/
PLAN.md

# tray launcher: the .lnk stores absolute paths - regenerate it per machine with
# misc/New-TrayShortcut.ps1 (the tray host refreshes it on launch)
/AgentHydra.lnk
/AgentHydra Instances.lnk
# The pre-rename shortcuts survive on machines that upgraded, until they are re-created.
/CCManagerUI.lnk
/CCManagerUI Instances.lnk

# Local root rebuild convenience wrapper (delegates to misc/rebuild_agenthydra.bat)
/rebuild_agenthydra.bat

# Owner handoff notes: internal, not for the public repo
docs/HANDOFF_MICHAEL.md

# Local AI memory for this repo. Deliberately NOT published.
/.claude/memory/

# ⛔ PUBLIC REPO: the to-do list is not published (owner directive, 2026-08-29).
# These notes are the most candid writing in the repo - what is broken, what is half-built, what is
# waiting on a person. The folder's own README stays tracked (it states the convention); only the
# items are ignored. docs/todo/TODO.md stays local, and the pre-push release gate
# (.githooks/check-public-push.mjs) reads it there.
/docs/todo/*
!/docs/todo/README.md

# bun test --parallel writes a per-file timing cache here to schedule the next run.
/timings.json

# A built or downloaded binary dropped at the repo root. `bun run dist` writes the real one to
# dist/ (ignored above); this is the copy people leave beside the checkout after downloading a
# release asset or hand-copying one out of dist/. It is ~100 MB, so an accidental `git add` here
# is expensive and irreversible on a public repo. Named exactly, NOT as a blanket *.exe, so a new
# kind of binary still shows up in `git status` and is a decision rather than an accident.
/AgentHydra.exe

# The Windows programs scripts/build-natives.ts builds from the Rust source beside them, into the
# places the app runs them from. They are built (by a PC, CI and every release), never committed: a
# committed copy cannot be traced to its source. `.old-<pid>` is a running copy a rebuild moved aside.
/misc/AgentHydra-Tray.exe
/misc/AgentHydra-Tray.exe.old-*
/misc/climayte-runner.exe
/misc/climayte-runner.exe.old-*
/desk2/launcher/HydraDesk2.exe
/desk2/launcher/HydraDesk2.exe.old-*

# The Codex hub's builds. codex-hub-tray/build.sh and build-macos.sh, and the commands in
# docs/REFERENCE.md write them to dist/ (ignored above); these catch one built beside its source,
# by a plain `go build` or a `bun build --compile` without --outfile. Each is 10 to 100 MB, and a
# tray build holds the operator's hub addresses. Named exactly, for the same reason as above.
/codex-hub-tray/codex-hub-tray
/codex-hub-tray/codex-hub-tray.exe
/codex-hub-tray/codex-hub-tray-*
/codex-hub-push*
/server/codex-hub-push*
# The private key the hub's builds are signed with (scripts/codex-hub-sign.ts keygen) is kept outside the checkout
# (docs/CODEX-HUB.md); this catches one made inside it anyway. No .key file is part of the repository.
*.key

# Local investigation write-ups: internal working notes, same convention as
# docs/HANDOFF_MICHAEL.md and /docs/todo/* above. Findings get upstreamed as a fix plus its
# comment, not as a file of field notes about one machine's logs.
/FINDINGS-*.md
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python build metadata (pip install -e .)
*.egg-info/

# HSwarm's native scanners: build output (hswarm native build)
hswarm/native/bin/
hswarm/native/zscan-rs/target/
hswarm/native/zscan-rs/build.log

# Docker hub host-side updater state (contains credentials and backups)
/deploy/docker/.hub-backups/
/deploy/docker/.hub-update.lock/
/deploy/docker/.env.new
